  "elements": [
    {
      "id": "1DuWuh9bWH7V2Xp1kdRDl",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 373.63671875,
      "y": 169.1796875,
      "width": 1462.9981689453125,
      "height": 450,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "aJ",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 198592823,
      "version": 1607,
      "versionNonce": 1979163287,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1776475543944,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Layers\n1. CPU Image decoder (File bytes -> raw pixel buffeer + (width, height, channels, format).\n    stb_image.h -> free lib for reading images into memory\n    Output RGBA8 even if source is RGB \n    Make sure sRBG correction at the end \n2. GPU Memory allocation\n3. GPU texture struct - A struct wrapping VkImage, VkImageView, VkSampler, the VMA Allocation, width, \n    height,format,current layout. \n    This works as a \"texture\" and is an abstraction -> create(), destroy(), resize(), updateContents()\n4. Upload/transfer layer - Staging buffer (HOST_MEMORY) -> vkCmdCopyBufferToImage -> image (DEVICE_LOCAL, SHARED_READ_ONLY_OPTIMAL). \n    Two layout transitions: UNDEFINED -> TRANSFER_DST_OPTIMAL, copy, then TRANSFER_DST_OPTIMAL -> SHADER_READ_ONLY_OPTIMAL. \n    Run this on a one-shot command buffer submitted to a transfer-capable queue, then fence-wait before the viewer tries to display.\n5. ImGui bridge. Wraps the pair (GPU texture resource, VkDescriptorSet).\n    ImGui_ImplVulkan_AddTexture(sampler, view, layout) returns the descriptor set; you hold it, pass it to ImGui::Image, and call\n    ImGui_ImplVulkan_RemoveTexture on cleanup. \n    Descriptor pool must have VK_DESCRIPTOR_POOL_CREATE_FREE_DESCRIPTOR_SET_BIT or RemoveTexture will fail\n\n    ",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Layers\n1. CPU Image decoder (File bytes -> raw pixel buffeer + (width, height, channels, format).\n    stb_image.h -> free lib for reading images into memory\n    Output RGBA8 even if source is RGB \n    Make sure sRBG correction at the end \n2. GPU Memory allocation\n3. GPU texture struct - A struct wrapping VkImage, VkImageView, VkSampler, the VMA Allocation, width, \n    height,format,current layout. \n    This works as a \"texture\" and is an abstraction -> create(), destroy(), resize(), updateContents()\n4. Upload/transfer layer - Staging buffer (HOST_MEMORY) -> vkCmdCopyBufferToImage -> image (DEVICE_LOCAL, SHARED_READ_ONLY_OPTIMAL). \n    Two layout transitions: UNDEFINED -> TRANSFER_DST_OPTIMAL, copy, then TRANSFER_DST_OPTIMAL -> SHADER_READ_ONLY_OPTIMAL. \n    Run this on a one-shot command buffer submitted to a transfer-capable queue, then fence-wait before the viewer tries to display.\n5. ImGui bridge. Wraps the pair (GPU texture resource, VkDescriptorSet).\n    ImGui_ImplVulkan_AddTexture(sampler, view, layout) returns the descriptor set; you hold it, pass it to ImGui::Image, and call\n    ImGui_ImplVulkan_RemoveTexture on cleanup. \n    Descriptor pool must have VK_DESCRIPTOR_POOL_CREATE_FREE_DESCRIPTOR_SET_BIT or RemoveTexture will fail\n\n    ",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
